<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">II </span><span id="S2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Methodology</span></h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This work proposes a two-stage reconstruction framework that integrates a diffusion-based generative prior with sparsity-promoting physical constraints, enabling robust and high-fidelity image recovery from limited or noisy measurements. The key notations used throughout this paper are summarized in Table <a href="#S1.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ I Introduction ‣ Diffusion–Low-Rank Hybrid Reconstruction for Sparse-View Medical Imaging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS0.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-</span>1 </span>Overall Framework</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proposed approach consists of two tightly coupled stages: <span id="S2.SS0.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 1:</span> An initial estimate is generated from pure noise using a diffusion model, specifically by solving an inverse stochastic differential equation (SDE). <span id="S2.SS0.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 2:</span> This estimate is further refined by enforcing both anisotropic total variation (TV) and low-rank (nuclear norm) regularization. The overall joint optimization is efficiently solved via the Alternating Direction Method of Multipliers (ADMM).
Throughout, ADMM iterations are embedded within the diffusion process, balancing data fidelity (<math id="S2.SS0.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{A}x-b\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{A}x-b\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) and learned priors, while leveraging GPU parallelization for computational efficiency.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS0.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-</span>2 </span>Diffusion Model: Forward and Reverse Processes</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forward Process (Variance-Exploding SDE):</span> The forward diffusion process gradually corrupts a clean image <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(0)</annotation></semantics></math> by adding Gaussian noise over time, resulting in a highly noisy sample <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(T)</annotation></semantics></math>. This process is formally described by the following SDE: <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}x=\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{d}\sigma^{2}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w},\quad t\in[0,T]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}x=\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{d}\sigma^{2}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w},\quad t\in[0,T],</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a monotonically increasing noise scale function, and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\mathbf{w}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes standard Brownian motion. Here, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(0)</annotation></semantics></math> is the clean image, and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(T)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}(T)\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(T)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}(T)\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximally corrupted image at terminal time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inverse (Reverse) Process:</span> To generate a clean image from noise, a time-dependent score function <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}(x,t)\approx\nabla_{x}\log p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}(x,t)\approx\nabla_{x}\log p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is learned, where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the data distribution at time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. The reverse-time SDE for denoising is: <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}x=\left[-\frac{1}{2}\frac{\mathrm{d}\sigma^{2}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}\,s_{\theta}(x,t)\right]\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{d}\sigma^{2}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}}\,\mathrm{d}\bar{\mathbf{w}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}x=\left[-\frac{1}{2}\frac{\mathrm{d}\sigma^{2}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}\,s_{\theta}(x,t)\right]\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{d}\sigma^{2}(t)}{\mathrm{d}t}}\,\mathrm{d}\bar{\mathbf{w}},</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}\bar{\mathbf{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\bar{\mathbf{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a standard Brownian increment in reverse time.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In practice, this SDE is discretized using the Euler–Maruyama scheme:</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i-1}=x_{i}+(\sigma_{i}^{2}-\sigma_{i-1}^{2})\,s_{\theta}(x_{i},t_{i})+\sqrt{\sigma_{i}^{2}-\sigma_{i-1}^{2}}\cdot z_{i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i-1}=x_{i}+(\sigma_{i}^{2}-\sigma_{i-1}^{2})\,s_{\theta}(x_{i},t_{i})+\sqrt{\sigma_{i}^{2}-\sigma_{i-1}^{2}}\cdot z_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and the time interval is divided into <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> steps, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t=T/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t=T/N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS0.SSS3.6" class="ltx_text">II-</span>3 </span>Joint Optimization Formulation</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reconstruction is posed as the minimization of the following composite objective:</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{x}\;\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{A}x-b\|_{2}^{2}+\lambda_{\mathrm{diff}}\bigl[-\log p_{\theta}(x)\bigr]+\alpha\,\mathrm{TV}(x)+\beta\|P(x)\|_{*}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>x</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>diff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TV</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{x}\;\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{A}x-b\|_{2}^{2}+\lambda_{\mathrm{diff}}\bigl[-\log p_{\theta}(x)\bigr]+\alpha\,\mathrm{TV}(x)+\beta\|P(x)\|_{*},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}x\approx b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}x\approx b</annotation></semantics></math> enforces data fidelity to measurements <math id="S2.SS0.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the diffusion generative prior, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is anisotropic total variation, and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|P(x)\|_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|P(x)\|_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the nuclear norm (low-rank) of the patch-wise unfolded image.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS0.SSS4.6" class="ltx_text">II-</span>4 </span>ADMM-Based Solution Strategy</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To efficiently handle the non-smooth TV and low-rank regularizations, we introduce auxiliary variables:1. <math id="S2.SS0.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{x}=\nabla_{x}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{x}=\nabla_{x}x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{y}=\nabla_{y}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{y}=\nabla_{y}x</annotation></semantics></math> (for image gradients), 2. <math id="S2.SS0.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=P(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=P(x)</annotation></semantics></math> (for low-rank patches). The constrained optimization problem is reformulated as:</p>
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{x,v_{x},v_{y},Z}\;\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{A}x-b\|_{2}^{2}+\alpha(\|v_{x}\|_{1}+\|v_{y}\|_{1})+\beta\|Z\|_{*}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{x,v_{x},v_{y},Z}\;\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{A}x-b\|_{2}^{2}+\alpha(\|v_{x}\|_{1}+\|v_{y}\|_{1})+\beta\|Z\|_{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{subject to:}\;\;v_{x}=\nabla_{x}x,\;\;v_{y}=\nabla_{y}x,\;\;Z=P(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>subject to:</mtext><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{subject to:}\;\;v_{x}=\nabla_{x}x,\;\;v_{y}=\nabla_{y}x,\;\;Z=P(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The augmented Lagrangian is then constructed, and the solution proceeds via the following ADMM updates:</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS0.SSS5.6" class="ltx_text">II-</span>5 </span>ADMM Iterative Updates</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Diffusion Denoising Step:</span>
Before each ADMM iteration, the reverse diffusion process is performed to refine <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> using the score network <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Image Variable Update (<math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-step):</span></p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{l}\left({{{\bf{A}}^{T}}{\bf{A}}+{\rho_{1}}\nabla_{x}^{T}{\nabla_{x}}+{\rho_{2}}\nabla_{y}^{T}{\nabla_{y}}+{\rho_{3}}I}\right){x^{k+1}}\\
\begin{array}[]{*{20}{c}}&amp;&amp;\end{array}={{\bf{A}}^{T}}b+{\rho_{1}}\nabla_{x}^{T}(v_{x}^{k}+u_{1}^{k})+{\rho_{2}}\nabla_{y}^{T}(v_{y}^{k}+u_{2}^{k})\\
\begin{array}[]{*{20}{c}}&amp;&amp;\end{array}+{\rho_{3}}({Z^{k}}+u_{3}^{k}),\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{l}\left({{{\bf{A}}^{T}}{\bf{A}}+{\rho_{1}}\nabla_{x}^{T}{\nabla_{x}}+{\rho_{2}}\nabla_{y}^{T}{\nabla_{y}}+{\rho_{3}}I}\right){x^{k+1}}\\
\begin{array}[]{*{20}{c}}&amp;&amp;\end{array}={{\bf{A}}^{T}}b+{\rho_{1}}\nabla_{x}^{T}(v_{x}^{k}+u_{1}^{k})+{\rho_{2}}\nabla_{y}^{T}(v_{y}^{k}+u_{2}^{k})\\
\begin{array}[]{*{20}{c}}&amp;&amp;\end{array}+{\rho_{3}}({Z^{k}}+u_{3}^{k}),\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are penalty parameters and <math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are scaled Lagrange multipliers.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gradient Variable Update (<math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>-step):</span></p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\leftarrow\operatorname{sign}(v)\odot\max(|v|-\tau,0)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\leftarrow\operatorname{sign}(v)\odot\max(|v|-\tau,0),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\alpha/\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\alpha/\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Low-Rank Variable Update (<math id="S2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>-step):</span>
For each patch matrix, update <math id="S2.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> via singular value thresholding (SVT):</p>
<table id="S2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}\leftarrow\max(\sigma_{i}-\beta/\rho,0)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}\leftarrow\max(\sigma_{i}-\beta/\rho,0),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I1.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and reconstruct <math id="S2.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=U\tilde{\Sigma}V^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=U\tilde{\Sigma}V^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lagrange Multiplier Update (<math id="S2.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>-step):</span></p>
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E7X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E7X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u_{1}^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u_{1}^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E7X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=u_{1}^{k}+\bigl(v_{x}^{k+1}-\nabla_{x}x^{k+1}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=u_{1}^{k}+\bigl(v_{x}^{k+1}-\nabla_{x}x^{k+1}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E7Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E7Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u_{2}^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u_{2}^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E7Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=u_{2}^{k}+\bigl(v_{y}^{k+1}-\nabla_{y}x^{k+1}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=u_{2}^{k}+\bigl(v_{y}^{k+1}-\nabla_{y}x^{k+1}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E7Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E7Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u_{3}^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u_{3}^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E7Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=u_{3}^{k}+\bigl(Z^{k+1}-P(x^{k+1})\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=u_{3}^{k}+\bigl(Z^{k+1}-P(x^{k+1})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This procedure is repeated until convergence. The overall energy decreases monotonically and, under mild convexity assumptions, the method converges with a rate of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(1/k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(1/k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By embedding the diffusion generative prior into the ADMM framework and explicitly balancing measurement consistency, noise suppression, edge preservation, and global low-rank structure, the proposed methodology achieves superior, diagnostically reliable image reconstructions, particularly under challenging, incomplete, or noisy data conditions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span><span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Diffusion–Low-Rank Hybrid Reconstruction for Sparse-View Medical Imaging</span></figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.6.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="alg1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Requires:<span id="alg1.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}^{*},\;b,\;A,\;\alpha,\;\beta,\;\rho_{1},\;\rho_{2},\;\rho_{3},\;\mathbf{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>𝐍</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}^{*},\;b,\;A,\;\alpha,\;\beta,\;\rho_{1},\;\rho_{2},\;\rho_{3},\;\mathbf{N}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Define:</span><span id="alg1.6.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{x},\;D_{y}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{x},\;D_{y}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.6.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Gradient operators in </span><math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.6.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">/</span><math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.6.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> directions</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Define:</span><span id="alg1.6.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(\cdot)\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\cdot)\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.6.3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Patch-unfolding operator that maps an image to a block matrix</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Define:</span><span id="alg1.6.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Shrink}(v,\tau)\leftarrow\operatorname{sign}(v)\!\odot\!\max(|v|-\tau,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Shrink</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.072em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.072em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Shrink}(v,\tau)\leftarrow\operatorname{sign}(v)\!\odot\!\max(|v|-\tau,0)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.6.4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (soft threshold)</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Define:</span><span id="alg1.6.5.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{SVT}(M,\tau)\!:\!M=U\Sigma V^{\!\top},\;U\!\operatorname{diag}(\max(\sigma_{i}-\tau,0))V^{\!\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">SVT</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.128em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.128em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">U</mi><mo lspace="0.017em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{SVT}(M,\tau)\!:\!M=U\Sigma V^{\!\top},\;U\!\operatorname{diag}(\max(\sigma_{i}-\tau,0))V^{\!\top}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="alg1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{0}\!\sim\!\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\sigma_{T}^{2}\bm{I});\;v_{x}^{0}\!\leftarrow\!0;\;v_{y}^{0}\!\leftarrow\!0;\;Z^{0}\!\leftarrow\!0;\;u_{1}^{0}\!\leftarrow\!0;\;u_{2}^{0}\!\leftarrow\!0;\;u_{3}^{0}\!\leftarrow\!0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.128em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.128em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">𝟎</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑰</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">;</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{0}\!\sim\!\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\sigma_{T}^{2}\bm{I});\;v_{x}^{0}\!\leftarrow\!0;\;v_{y}^{0}\!\leftarrow\!0;\;Z^{0}\!\leftarrow\!0;\;u_{1}^{0}\!\leftarrow\!0;\;u_{2}^{0}\!\leftarrow\!0;\;u_{3}^{0}\!\leftarrow\!0.</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
